WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.719
Part 3

00:00:01.719 --> 00:00:04.080
Thank you, Chairman.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:12.480
Just to reinforce some of the things that
the Chairman was saying earlier on, we are

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:19.180
now in a position where most of our staff
have been appointed; most are in post now.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.029
I know that Jo is going to talk about some
of the HR issues later.

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:29.490
We made a commitment as an executive team
to go out and meet our staff, both in a national

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:36.690
support centre, but more widely in each of
the area teams over the period.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.280
By the end of May we will have done almost
every area team.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.829
Feedback
I think there are two or three things I would

00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:46.770
say about that in terms of the feedback that
I am getting from it and where we are.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:52.399
Just to reinforce, again, the point that the
Chairman made about the number of staff that

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:59.120
we have is actually half the number that were
doing the jobs that they were doing in the

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.280
previous arrangement.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:08.360
A massive effort of job redesign and service
redesign is required to enable us to deliver

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.360
the efficiencies.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:17.610
That has contributed itself over half a billion
pounds worth of savings which are being reinvested

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:23.880
in frontline services, so a big but really
important thing for us to do as part of these

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:24.880
changes.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:30.400
Abolition of SHAs and PCTs
We have been visiting the area teams and for

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.741
those people, in particular, who were either
working in SHAs and PCTs, I think you have

00:01:35.741 --> 00:01:41.840
to recognise the journey that they have all
been on.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:49.020
Since the government announced the abolition
of SHAs and PCTs, not only have they had to

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:54.900
build the new organisation, they have also
had to make sure that the NHS continued to

00:01:54.900 --> 00:02:00.270
improved services for patients, and at the
same time of being extraordinarily worried

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:08.129
about their own circumstances of applying
for jobs, and I think genuinely did an extraordinary

00:02:08.129 --> 00:02:10.920
job during that period.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:16.240
The thing I would say about having been to
those meetings is that people are now ready

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.151
to do something new, because most of them
now are doing the single job that they have

00:02:21.151 --> 00:02:24.820
been employed to do as opposed to the two
or three jobs that some people were doing,

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:29.250
I think there is an enormous energy and enthusiasm
to take things forward.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:35.390
This is, in a sense, a moment in time for
NHS England, and that is why it is so important

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:41.280
when we talk later about getting the vision
and the objectives of the organisation right,

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.700
that we can mobilise people to make great
improvements and outcomes for patients.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:51.260
So a really positive set of experiences for
me going round.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:55.110
Not to say that there are not operational
problems, and there are, where you look at

00:02:55.110 --> 00:03:00.090
the way some of the HR practices work, the
implementation of IT, all of those things,

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:04.240
but nevertheless I think people are enthused
and want to get on and improve services for

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.430
patients so really reassuring from that perspective.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:10.650
National clinical directors
We have also brought together an important

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:15.560
group of people for NHS England, which is
the national clinical directors.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:23.590
We have appointed 25 national clinical directors
across the country covering almost every specialty

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:33.070
and care group that you could imagine, from
psychiatry right the way through to diabetes

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:39.030
and obesity, so a fantastic array of people
that we have.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.350
25 people, all working part time.

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:46.440
It is important for those people that they
continue to do their clinical work so they

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:52.610
are in touch with clinical practices as they
go along; really important that they do that.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:54.760
We have brought them together as part of an
induction programme.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:04:00.860
Again, we have a fantastic resource there,
not only for NHS England, but for the NHS

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:05.341
widely where you have a whole set of people
who have significant national, and in some

00:04:05.341 --> 00:04:45.560
cases international reputations for the kind
of clinical work that they 

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:52.850
have done.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:05:09.960
They 
will be able to provide support and help to

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:38.240
the service chains 
that we need in the NHS 

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:59.690
going forward, and a really valuable asset,
I think, for us as we go forward.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:20.840
Interventions
I should 

00:06:20.840 --> 00:07:10.960
say a thing about a couple of interventions
that we 

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:12.160
will be making next week

